    {
      "id": "M13-HTTP-TX",
      "priority": 1,
      "bounded_change": "Add a new exact-SDK6.0.2 build-local generator that only ensures a released request buffer is reallocated at original client->buffer_size_tx before request generation, and appends one same-owner synchronous completed-GET release API. Do not modify installed SDK or import SDK6.1 strict-header/auth/redirect changes. Parent has authorized a prototype/new-tool host proof only; production CMake/header/callsite integration is deferred until agreed.",
      "ownership_contract": "Release only non-null client/request/buffer, synchronous GET, post_len==0,data_write_left==0,state==RES_ON_DATA_START. Idempotent NULL data release. Retain request header dictionary, URL/query/auth data, response RX/raw/cached body and borrowed post_data. Reuse allocates original configured capacity before any sender dereference; allocation failure returns NO_MEM before writing and keeps the released state retryable. Partial/async/header-sent/POST/body states must reject release. Same owner task only; no concurrent client use.",
      "expected_effect": "Current CYD radio requests4096TX bytes: release that requested payload after final accepted headers, without reducing URLs/header capacity or TLS record size. Exact heap usable-size/fragmentation benefit remains to measure; do not claim exact physical4096byte heap gain.",
      "proposed_owned_paths": [
        "tools/patch_cyd_http_request_buffer.py",
        "tests/run-cyd-http-request-buffer.py",
        "tests/native/cyd_http_request_buffer/test.c"
      ],
      "required_executable_evidence": [
        "Exact raw or LF-normalized SDK6.0.2 guard accepts pinned source; wrong/mutated source and already-patched source reject; unmodified input bytes recover exactly after removing only the two inserted spans.",
        "Actual SDK6.0.2 request preparation/sender plus real http_header/http_utils compile under strict host warnings and ASan/UBSan. No copied mocked sender implementation.",
        "Long URL and paginated headers preserve exact wire bytes across release/reuse; repeated release/cleanup has no double free; reallocation OOM retries without partial wire output.",
        "Async partial write/body/POST/auth-redirect retry preparation states retain their live TX storage; released GET may reuse for subsequent GET/POST at full capacity, preserving untouched dictionaries/body and response bytes.",
        "Named semantic controls detect missing reallocation, premature release/borrowed body corruption and duplicate frees by a semantic oracle rather than accepting a sanitizer crash.",
        "Later production integration: actual stream owner release only after open_stream final accepted headers; current redirect chain, auth, Stop/EOF/maintenance and all SDK build/backend gates remain required."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "M13-IDLE-RECLAIM",
      "priority": 2,
      "bounded_change": "Extract a small optional shared allocation-pressure wrapper around esp_mbedtls_mem_calloc that reclaims only shared adaptive queue idle slots above its existing minimum, retries a bounded number of allocations and otherwise delegates unchanged. No permanent static TLS slot, dynamic-buffer toggle,32KiB headroom or IRAM change.",
      "ownership_contract": "Bind a queue only after CYD startup has fully succeeded and its lifetime is retained; leave NULL throughout rollback/failure. If future runtime teardown is introduced, provide detach/inflight reference protocol before queue destruction. On SMP, concurrent TLS contexts and consumer returns must never use a freed queue or hold allocator calls under queue lock. Keep calloc zero/overflow semantics, queued bytes and producer/consumer/control leases.",
      "required_executable_evidence": [
        "Actual wrapper+shared queue concurrent host tests cover busy producer/consumer/FIFO/control lease preservation, overflow/zero delegate behavior, repeated allocator failure, bounded reclaim and restore only by stream owner between connections.",
        "Actual CYD startup failure at every gate leaves hook unbound; actual successful publication precedes any hook use; expose narrow snapshot counters without logging/allocating in hooks.",
        "Link/ELF evidence for pinned Xtensa archive references confirms __wrap calloc chain and absence of new unexpected allocator paths.",
        "TLS/WebUI/OTA concurrent contexts and all-codec physical memory peaks/jitter need measurement before default enablement."
      ],
